1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,460
Once upon a time, there was a man who died.

2
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:08,100
The story was interrupted.

3
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:13,360
Along with his heart, the prince lost his kindness towards other people,

4
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,900
and even his memories of having fought bravely.

5
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:21,440
Meanwhile, scattered throughout the town,

6
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:26,080
the shards of the prince's heart sought places to settle,

7
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:30,540
and found their way into people's hearts which had a void in them.

8
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:33,580
Among those possessed by the shards

9
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:37,580
were some who ended up making their own tales go awry.

10
00:02:25,354 --> 00:02:30,354
I really and truly have been able to become Princess Tutu.

11
00:02:32,354 --> 00:02:34,354
Tuck your chin in!

12
00:02:36,354 --> 00:02:38,354
It's no laughing matter!

13
00:02:38,354 --> 00:02:41,354
If you can't even do that, then you'll never get off probation!

14
00:02:41,354 --> 00:02:42,354
Stop it!

15
00:02:42,354 --> 00:02:44,354
Now be reasonable!

16
00:02:44,354 --> 00:02:47,354
Duck simply isn't capable of doing two things at once!

17
00:02:47,354 --> 00:02:49,354
All she has to do is walk with a book on her head!

18
00:02:49,354 --> 00:02:52,354
If it's something so simple she can't do it, she simply can't!

19
00:02:52,354 --> 00:02:54,354
Then she'll never be a prima ballerina!

20
00:02:54,354 --> 00:02:56,354
No, she won't! She couldn't possibly become one!

21
00:02:56,354 --> 00:02:58,354
Stop saying such awful things!

22
00:02:59,354 --> 00:03:01,354
Oh, look how hurt she is!

23
00:03:01,354 --> 00:03:03,354
Come on, smile, huh?

24
00:03:03,354 --> 00:03:04,354
Hey, it's your fault!

25
00:03:04,354 --> 00:03:05,354
No way!

26
00:03:05,354 --> 00:03:10,354
But for someone on probation, Duck sure has been acting weird and goofy smiley all day!

27
00:03:10,354 --> 00:03:11,354
She's always been weird!

28
00:03:11,354 --> 00:03:13,354
I mean more than usual!

29
00:03:13,354 --> 00:03:14,354
Now that you say it!

30
00:03:14,354 --> 00:03:15,354
What?

31
00:03:15,354 --> 00:03:17,354
Did something happen?

32
00:03:17,354 --> 00:03:19,354
No, not really!

33
00:03:19,354 --> 00:03:20,354
Liar!

34
00:03:20,354 --> 00:03:22,354
Not that there was anything, but...

35
00:03:22,354 --> 00:03:24,354
So there was!

36
00:03:24,354 --> 00:03:25,354
Uh, well...

37
00:03:25,354 --> 00:03:26,354
Come on, Duck!

38
00:03:26,354 --> 00:03:27,354
Sit it out!

39
00:03:27,354 --> 00:03:28,354
Um...

40
00:03:28,354 --> 00:03:29,354
Uh...

41
00:03:29,354 --> 00:03:30,354
So yeah, this dream?

42
00:03:30,354 --> 00:03:32,354
It's about this one dream that I had.

43
00:03:32,354 --> 00:03:35,354
See, there's this really strong and handsome prince in it?

44
00:03:35,354 --> 00:03:38,354
But this prince is fighting against an evil raven!

45
00:03:38,354 --> 00:03:41,354
He can steal the raven away if he shatters his own heart!

46
00:03:41,354 --> 00:03:44,354
But when he loses his heart, he also loses his feelings!

47
00:03:44,354 --> 00:03:47,354
And the prince's eyes always look so lonely!

48
00:03:47,354 --> 00:03:48,354
And for this prince...

49
00:03:48,354 --> 00:03:49,354
Is that all?

50
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:50,354
What?

51
00:03:50,354 --> 00:03:52,354
Hey, I've heard a story like that before!

52
00:03:52,354 --> 00:03:53,354
Story?

53
00:03:53,354 --> 00:03:55,354
It's from the prince and the raven!

54
00:03:55,354 --> 00:03:56,354
Huh?

55
00:03:56,354 --> 00:03:57,354
Here.

56
00:03:57,354 --> 00:03:58,354
This book, right?

57
00:03:58,354 --> 00:04:03,354
The prince was a wholehearted hero who fought the demonic raven!

58
00:04:03,354 --> 00:04:06,354
Well, he was when they were still inside the story!

59
00:04:06,354 --> 00:04:07,354
Um...

60
00:04:07,354 --> 00:04:09,354
What's the name of the guy who wrote the story?

61
00:04:09,354 --> 00:04:10,354
His name?

62
00:04:10,354 --> 00:04:11,354
It's Drosselmeyer!

63
00:04:11,354 --> 00:04:12,354
Don't you know?

64
00:04:12,354 --> 00:04:13,354
No!

65
00:04:13,354 --> 00:04:14,354
I had no idea!

66
00:04:14,354 --> 00:04:17,354
This is no time for silly books and stupid grins!

67
00:04:17,354 --> 00:04:19,354
Two books are too much for you, Duck!

68
00:04:19,354 --> 00:04:22,354
Make sure you can do it by the end of the day!

69
00:04:22,354 --> 00:04:23,354
Good luck!

70
00:04:23,354 --> 00:04:24,354
You've got nothing to lose!

71
00:04:24,354 --> 00:04:26,354
Don't you dare slack off!

72
00:04:26,354 --> 00:04:27,354
Oh!

73
00:04:27,354 --> 00:04:31,354
So this Drosselmeyer person, does he live somewhere in this town?

74
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:32,354
Huh?

75
00:04:32,354 --> 00:04:33,354
No way!

76
00:04:33,354 --> 00:04:34,354
He died ages ago!

77
00:04:34,354 --> 00:04:35,354
What?

78
00:04:35,354 --> 00:04:39,354
The story ends part of the way through, too!

79
00:04:39,354 --> 00:04:40,354
Oh yeah!

80
00:04:40,354 --> 00:04:43,354
Didn't he like die while he was writing the book or something?

81
00:04:43,354 --> 00:04:44,354
What?

82
00:04:44,354 --> 00:04:45,354
Yes!

83
00:04:45,354 --> 00:04:50,354
He came out of the story I wrote and ended up losing his heart to seal the raven away!

84
00:04:50,354 --> 00:04:56,354
That means the person writing the story died and the characters in the story came out?

85
00:04:56,354 --> 00:04:58,354
Something that strange!

86
00:04:58,354 --> 00:05:02,354
But I guess it isn't as strange as a duck turning into a person!

87
00:05:02,354 --> 00:05:07,354
So that would mean that Senior Muto is actually a prince out of a story!

88
00:05:07,354 --> 00:05:10,354
That must be why he's so handsome then!

89
00:05:10,354 --> 00:05:11,354
Hm?

90
00:05:11,354 --> 00:05:12,354
It's Rue!

91
00:05:12,354 --> 00:05:15,354
I wonder if she knows about this?

92
00:05:15,354 --> 00:05:16,354
Oh!

93
00:05:16,354 --> 00:05:18,354
It's Senior Muto!

94
00:05:18,354 --> 00:05:22,354
So, he's going on a picnic with Rue.

95
00:05:22,354 --> 00:05:23,354
Lucky her.

96
00:05:23,354 --> 00:05:28,354
But you know, when you get right down to it, I'm just a duck.

97
00:05:28,354 --> 00:05:30,354
Maybe I'll practice or something.

98
00:05:30,354 --> 00:05:31,354
Hey!

99
00:05:31,354 --> 00:05:32,354
Have you seen Muto around?

100
00:05:32,354 --> 00:05:35,354
Is something the matter with Senior Muto?

101
00:05:35,354 --> 00:05:38,354
He went out without even telling me about it.

102
00:05:38,354 --> 00:05:40,354
Gee, who cares about that?

103
00:05:40,354 --> 00:05:42,354
He's Rue's boyfriend after all.

104
00:05:42,354 --> 00:05:43,354
What?

105
00:05:43,354 --> 00:05:44,354
So he's with Rue?

106
00:05:44,354 --> 00:05:45,354
Huh?

107
00:05:45,354 --> 00:05:46,354
Where'd they go?

108
00:05:46,354 --> 00:05:47,354
Tell me!

109
00:05:47,354 --> 00:05:48,354
I don't know!

110
00:05:48,354 --> 00:05:49,354
Don't lie to me!

111
00:05:49,354 --> 00:05:50,354
It's the truth!

112
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:56,354
Oh, I wonder if he knows about Senior Muto.

113
00:05:56,354 --> 00:06:01,354
Say, do you happen to know the story of the prince and the raven?

114
00:06:01,354 --> 00:06:02,354
What about it?

115
00:06:02,354 --> 00:06:06,354
Oh, well, um, nothing really about it.

116
00:06:06,354 --> 00:06:08,354
A tale for children and nothing more.

117
00:06:13,354 --> 00:06:17,354
Hmm, acting so high and mighty, he doesn't even have a clue.

118
00:06:18,354 --> 00:06:21,354
So Senior Muto is a prince from inside a story.

119
00:06:21,354 --> 00:06:24,354
And I'm the only one who knows about it.

120
00:06:24,354 --> 00:06:27,354
It's up to me to protect my prince.

121
00:06:29,354 --> 00:06:31,354
I'm not playing hooky, I'm just taking a break.

122
00:06:31,354 --> 00:06:32,354
I'm allowed to do that.

123
00:06:32,354 --> 00:06:37,354
Besides, if I see Senior Muto and Rue, I can tell them that nasty guy was looking for them.

124
00:06:37,354 --> 00:06:40,354
I wonder if it's okay to tell them, though.

125
00:06:40,354 --> 00:06:42,354
Truth is a shy little thing.

126
00:06:42,354 --> 00:06:44,354
If you approach, it will hide.

127
00:06:44,354 --> 00:06:45,354
Miss Edo?

128
00:06:45,354 --> 00:06:47,354
Truth is a handsome little thing.

129
00:06:47,354 --> 00:06:50,354
If you run away, it will give chase.

130
00:06:50,354 --> 00:06:51,354
Huh?

131
00:06:51,354 --> 00:06:53,354
Having doubts, are you?

132
00:06:53,354 --> 00:06:55,354
Well, uh, I am.

133
00:06:55,354 --> 00:07:00,354
So you see, there's this person and there's another person who's really good friends with that person.

134
00:07:00,354 --> 00:07:02,354
And that person also has another good friend.

135
00:07:02,354 --> 00:07:05,354
But that person's friends aren't exactly friends with one another.

136
00:07:05,354 --> 00:07:07,354
Do you understand what I'm trying to say?

137
00:07:07,354 --> 00:07:14,354
A mighty wind can fan flames and make treetops sway, but flames burn trees to the ground.

138
00:07:14,354 --> 00:07:17,354
So, wind and flames and trees, huh?

139
00:07:17,354 --> 00:07:20,354
Does that mean that they can never get along with each other?

140
00:07:20,354 --> 00:07:21,354
Who's to say?

141
00:07:21,354 --> 00:07:22,354
Huh.

142
00:07:22,354 --> 00:07:27,354
But if the wind was too strong, it would put out the fire and topple all the trees.

143
00:07:27,354 --> 00:07:28,354
So that means...

144
00:07:28,354 --> 00:07:30,354
I don't get it.

145
00:07:30,354 --> 00:07:32,354
Well, thanks anyway, Miss Edo.

146
00:07:44,354 --> 00:07:45,354
Hmm.

147
00:07:45,354 --> 00:07:48,354
If it's a picnic, maybe they're at this park.

148
00:07:48,354 --> 00:07:49,354
Huh?

149
00:07:49,354 --> 00:07:51,354
Hey, there they are.

150
00:07:51,354 --> 00:07:52,354
Miyuto.

151
00:07:52,354 --> 00:07:53,354
What?

152
00:07:53,354 --> 00:07:55,354
I want to hear you say that you love me.

153
00:07:55,354 --> 00:07:56,354
Wow!

154
00:07:56,354 --> 00:07:57,354
Wow!

155
00:07:57,354 --> 00:07:58,354
What should I do?

156
00:07:58,354 --> 00:07:59,354
Should I go back?

157
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:00,354
I should go back, Shinrai.

158
00:08:00,354 --> 00:08:01,354
I'm going back now.

159
00:08:01,354 --> 00:08:02,354
Yes, Ru.

160
00:08:02,354 --> 00:08:03,354
I love you.

161
00:08:03,354 --> 00:08:04,354
Really?

162
00:08:04,354 --> 00:08:06,354
I really love you.

163
00:08:06,354 --> 00:08:11,354
I'm feeling thirsty.

164
00:08:11,354 --> 00:08:16,354
Huh?

165
00:08:16,354 --> 00:08:20,354
I think I would like to drink some water.

166
00:08:20,354 --> 00:08:21,354
Get it for me?

167
00:08:21,354 --> 00:08:22,354
Yes.

168
00:08:22,354 --> 00:08:23,354
Huh?

169
00:08:23,354 --> 00:08:24,354
Oh!

170
00:08:24,354 --> 00:08:25,354
He's coming this way.

171
00:08:25,354 --> 00:08:26,354
What do I do?

172
00:08:26,354 --> 00:08:27,354
He might see me!

173
00:08:27,354 --> 00:08:29,354
Man, they really are perfect for each other.

174
00:08:29,354 --> 00:08:39,354
But they didn't look like they were having very much fun out there.

175
00:08:39,354 --> 00:08:41,354
If he said something like that to me.

176
00:08:41,354 --> 00:08:42,354
Like that.

177
00:08:42,354 --> 00:08:46,354
Hello, duck.

178
00:08:46,354 --> 00:08:50,354
You know I love you, don't you?

179
00:08:50,354 --> 00:08:54,354
I really do.

180
00:08:54,354 --> 00:08:55,354
Oh!

181
00:08:55,354 --> 00:08:56,354
Excuse.

182
00:08:56,354 --> 00:08:57,354
Oh, it's in your mute hole.

183
00:08:57,354 --> 00:08:58,354
Hello!

184
00:08:58,354 --> 00:08:59,354
Um, the weather's pretty nice today, huh?

185
00:08:59,354 --> 00:09:01,354
So it may be bright during the day, but I'm sure it'll be dark at night.

186
00:09:01,354 --> 00:09:02,354
Ha!

187
00:09:02,354 --> 00:09:03,354
Stupid me!

188
00:09:03,354 --> 00:09:04,354
What am I stating the obvious for?

189
00:09:04,354 --> 00:09:05,354
I gotta say something funny!

190
00:09:05,354 --> 00:09:06,354
Oh, you know what?

191
00:09:06,354 --> 00:09:07,354
I really love taking walks, and you really love Ru, right?

192
00:09:07,354 --> 00:09:08,354
Oh, man!

193
00:09:08,354 --> 00:09:09,354
What the heck am I saying?

194
00:09:09,354 --> 00:09:11,354
Probably.

195
00:09:11,354 --> 00:09:25,354
Uh, probably?

196
00:09:25,354 --> 00:09:28,354
I guess I don't really understand what love is.

197
00:09:28,354 --> 00:09:30,354
But Ru and Fakir are the only ones who will tell me what to do, so I...

198
00:09:30,354 --> 00:09:32,354
You don't understand love?

199
00:09:32,354 --> 00:09:33,354
Senior Muto?

200
00:09:33,354 --> 00:09:34,354
Uh...

201
00:09:34,354 --> 00:09:35,354
Muto's fine.

202
00:09:35,354 --> 00:09:37,354
Muto's fine.

203
00:09:37,354 --> 00:09:41,354
Ah! Senior Muto! I mean Muto, your hand!

204
00:09:41,354 --> 00:09:44,354
Does it hurt?

205
00:09:44,354 --> 00:09:47,354
No. So then why the weird face?

206
00:09:47,354 --> 00:09:50,354
Is it really a weird face?

207
00:09:50,354 --> 00:09:53,354
But you're hurt, Muto!

208
00:09:53,354 --> 00:09:56,354
Fakir and Rue don't say things like that.

209
00:09:56,354 --> 00:10:01,354
It's the prince's eyes. The poor prince who lost his heart.

210
00:10:01,354 --> 00:10:06,354
That's why he doesn't know his own feelings, not even about loving or hurting.

211
00:10:06,354 --> 00:10:08,354
Then I'll do my best!

212
00:10:08,354 --> 00:10:10,354
At what?

213
00:10:10,354 --> 00:10:17,354
Oh, that is nothing in particular, but rather I want to work super hard at all sorts of things and write that injury!

214
00:10:17,354 --> 00:10:20,354
It'll get worse if you don't wash it properly.

215
00:10:20,354 --> 00:10:23,354
Thank goodness it's nothing too bad.

216
00:10:23,354 --> 00:10:28,354
Ah! The water that you went and got!

217
00:10:28,354 --> 00:10:32,354
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry! I'll go get some more!

218
00:10:32,354 --> 00:10:35,354
That being said, river water just wouldn't cut it.

219
00:10:35,354 --> 00:10:38,354
Rue deserves good tasting water after all.

220
00:10:38,354 --> 00:10:41,354
Water from these houses wouldn't work either, right?

221
00:10:41,354 --> 00:10:44,354
Where should I get it from?

222
00:10:44,354 --> 00:10:46,354
Oh, am I not in town?

223
00:10:46,354 --> 00:10:48,354
Guess I must have walked too far.

224
00:10:48,354 --> 00:10:53,354
Ah! Muto! I'll just go get the water, so you just stay right here and I'll be right back!

225
00:10:53,354 --> 00:10:55,354
Wait, I mean, where could I find water?

226
00:10:55,354 --> 00:10:57,354
Oh, right there.

227
00:10:57,354 --> 00:10:58,354
Huh?

228
00:10:58,354 --> 00:11:00,354
Oh, that's a restaurant!

229
00:11:00,354 --> 00:11:03,354
Some restaurant water would be perfect, huh?

230
00:11:03,354 --> 00:11:04,354
Maybe.

231
00:11:05,354 --> 00:11:07,354
Open...

232
00:11:07,354 --> 00:11:09,354
Ebine.

233
00:11:09,354 --> 00:11:11,354
I wonder if that's the restaurant's name.

234
00:11:13,354 --> 00:11:14,354
Excuse me!

235
00:11:14,354 --> 00:11:15,354
Yes?

236
00:11:15,354 --> 00:11:18,354
Well, this is a restaurant, right?

237
00:11:18,354 --> 00:11:21,354
Yes! Yes, it is!

238
00:11:21,354 --> 00:11:22,354
Ah!

239
00:11:22,354 --> 00:11:23,354
One moment, please!

240
00:11:26,354 --> 00:11:28,354
Thank you for waiting!

241
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:29,354
Welcome!

242
00:11:29,354 --> 00:11:31,354
I am the owner and chef here, Ebine.

243
00:11:31,354 --> 00:11:32,354
Um...

244
00:11:32,354 --> 00:11:33,354
How did you find out about this place?

245
00:11:33,354 --> 00:11:34,354
Did a friend tell you?

246
00:11:34,354 --> 00:11:35,354
No.

247
00:11:35,354 --> 00:11:37,354
And did you go out of your way to find it?

248
00:11:37,354 --> 00:11:38,354
No, not at all.

249
00:11:38,354 --> 00:11:40,354
It was a pure chance now, huh?

250
00:11:40,354 --> 00:11:41,354
Oh, yeah!

251
00:11:41,354 --> 00:11:43,354
How very splendid!

252
00:11:43,354 --> 00:11:46,354
I've never had a customer like that before!

253
00:11:46,354 --> 00:11:47,354
Now, please, sit down!

254
00:11:47,354 --> 00:11:50,354
Ma'am, I'm not a customer.

255
00:11:50,354 --> 00:11:52,354
Not a customer?

256
00:11:52,354 --> 00:11:54,354
I came for water.

257
00:11:54,354 --> 00:11:56,354
Just for some water?

258
00:11:56,354 --> 00:11:57,354
I...

259
00:11:57,354 --> 00:11:58,354
That is...

260
00:11:58,354 --> 00:11:59,354
I'm so sorry!

261
00:11:59,354 --> 00:12:02,354
You're hungry, aren't you?

262
00:12:02,354 --> 00:12:03,354
Uh...

263
00:12:03,354 --> 00:12:05,354
Then why not have a nice meal while you're here?

264
00:12:05,354 --> 00:12:06,354
Uh...

265
00:12:06,354 --> 00:12:07,354
What?

266
00:12:07,354 --> 00:12:08,354
But I don't have any money!

267
00:12:08,354 --> 00:12:09,354
That's fine!

268
00:12:09,354 --> 00:12:10,354
It doesn't matter!

269
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:11,354
Oh, yes!

270
00:12:11,354 --> 00:12:13,354
I just made some shrimp paté!

271
00:12:13,354 --> 00:12:15,354
The pendant gloved just now!

272
00:12:15,354 --> 00:12:18,354
But does that mean she has one of the shards with her?

273
00:12:32,354 --> 00:12:37,354
Where did Muto go?

274
00:12:37,354 --> 00:12:38,354
I don't know.

275
00:12:38,354 --> 00:12:41,354
Don't ever take him out without telling me.

276
00:12:41,354 --> 00:12:43,354
Muto doesn't belong to you.

